# fleet-roster.env.template — versioned REFERENCE for the fleet-wide
# declared-manager roster (Rick, 2026-06-11; user-level migration 2026-06-22).
#
# ── WHERE THE LIVE FILE LIVES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This TEMPLATE is the git-tracked, versioned canonical roster. The LIVE source
# is repo-agnostic and user-level: ~/.claude/fleet-roster.env (alongside
# settings.json + the per-project memory dirs), so NO product repo owns the
# fleet roster. Rick creates/edits the live file from this reference.
#
# ── ONE definition, two readers (both read the LIVE ~/.claude path) ────────────
#   (a) src/scripts/start-cc-with-tmux.sh — sources $HOME/.claude/fleet-roster.env
#       (set -a) and forwards every COSA_VOICE_MANAGERS__* variable into new tmux
#       sessions via -e (a generic compgen glob), so the SessionStart hook sees
#       the WHOLE fleet roster regardless of which repo the session is for.
#   (b) the arbiter systemd drop-in
#       (~/.config/systemd/user/lupin-arbiter-app.service.d/override.conf) —
#       loads it via `EnvironmentFile=-$HOME/.claude/fleet-roster.env`.
#
# Format: plain KEY="value" lines + # comments — the intersection of what
# `bash source` and systemd EnvironmentFile= both parse. No `export`, no
# variable expansion (no `$`), no embedded quotes or backslashes.
#
# Applying a roster change:
#   - live file:  edit ~/.claude/fleet-roster.env (copy from this template)
#   - interactive CC: next start-cc-with-tmux.sh launch picks it up (or
#     `set -a; source ~/.claude/fleet-roster.env; set +a` in an open shell)
#   - arbiter: systemctl --user daemon-reload && systemctl --user restart lupin-arbiter-app
#
# Semantics: COSA_VOICE_MANAGERS__<PROJECT> is a comma-separated persona-name
# roster. ORDER MATTERS — the roster HEAD is the declared fallback manager.
# Declaration is role-only for fleet status/escalation, PLUS reserve-from-random
# at allocation: declared names are excluded from random + chain-`*` persona
# allocation (still claimable by an explicit strict request or named chain
# element — that is how managers get their names). The subagent-governance hook
# also DERIVES its manager predicate from this roster (union across every
# COSA_VOICE_MANAGERS__* line) plus each COSA_VOICE_PREFERRED_PERSONA__* head.
#
# Optional bare-terminal coverage (sessions started without this script):
# add to ~/.bashrc:  set -a; source ~/.claude/fleet-roster.env; set +a
#
# Design: src/rnd/v0.1.8/2026.06.11-fleet-roster-env-file-and-reserve-from-random.md
#         src/rnd/2026.06.22-fleet-roster-to-user-level-migration-spec.md (PIP, María)
# (user-specific values like LUPIN_DEV_EMAIL do NOT belong here — they stay
# as literals in the systemd drop-in.)
#
# NOTE: the per-repo persona VALUES below are the versioned reference; Rick
# confirms the authoritative live roster at ~/.claude file-creation time.

COSA_VOICE_MANAGERS__LUPIN="Mr. Radio, Tiberius"
COSA_VOICE_MANAGERS__PLAN="María"
COSA_VOICE_MANAGERS__LOOKML="Sam"
COSA_VOICE_MANAGERS__LUPIN_MOBILE="Tiffany"
